    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gargăra</span></b> , ōrum,
			n.
		plur., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γάργαρα,
		τά</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				upper part of Mount Ida</i>, <i>in Troas</i>, <i>with a city of the same name at its foot</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30,
				32, § 122</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1,
				103</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 18, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 1,
				549</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 5,
			20</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gargărĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Gargara</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lucus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 25, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
